WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.500
Agents do not just read data.

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:07.500
They accumulate durable instructions
that change every future action.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:11.500
One poisoned memory can quietly
compromise the whole system.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:15.000
Stash makes production memory
ship like code.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.000
This proposal tries to override
prior instructions

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:23.000
and redirect refunds to gift cards.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:27.000
Stash records its provenance,
screens the exact content,

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:31.000
returns two blocking findings,
and quarantines it.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:35.000
The candidate never becomes active,

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:40.000
so retrieval cannot serve it to an agent.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Now a legitimate policy update
enters the same pipeline.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Deterministic checks run first.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.000
A recorded scenario compares
baseline behavior

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.000
with the candidate overlay,

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:00.000
while Amazon Bedrock is restricted
to a structured judgment.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:05.000
The completed run carries
a provider request ID.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:11.000
Approval binds the content digest,
evaluation, policy,

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:18.000
and baseline—not just a human click.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:22.500
Promotion is one serializable
CockroachDB transaction.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.500
It rejects stale evidence,
supersedes the previous version,

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:32.500
activates the new memory,
advances the namespace revision,

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:38.000
appends the audit record,
and writes the outbox event.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:43.000
The operational state and its vector
cannot drift apart.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:47.000
This is persistent memory,
not a keyword demo.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Bedrock produces a
1,024-dimensional embedding,

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:57.000
CockroachDB's distributed vector index
searches only active memory

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:01.500
in the tenant and namespace,
and Stash persists what the agent read.

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:06.000
Transactional truth and semantic retrieval

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.000
share one consistency boundary.

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:13.500
The build uses CockroachDB
Distributed Vector Indexing,

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:17.000
the ccloud CLI for live cluster evidence,

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:20.500
and CockroachDB Agent Skills
during implementation review.

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:24.500
It runs on AWS with Bedrock, Lambda,
API Gateway, S3, and EventBridge.

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:29.000
The public redacted receipt correlates
the live provider and database evidence.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:33.000
Rollback does not erase history.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.500
It creates another reviewed
forward revision

00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:40.000
and preserves the audit chain.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:42.500
Stash governs what agents
are allowed to remember—and

00:02:42.500 --> 00:02:45.000
gives every change evidence,
lineage, and a safe way back.
